It's not completely irrelevant. The "recently broken item" is a
shortcut for naming that particular item, so the rules for lost items
determine which item is selected by the shortcut. (It's only relevant in
terms of interface behaviour, though, because NetHack 4 allows
type-naming types of items that aren't in your inventory via
specifying their description. In 3.4.3, it's relevant in terms of
gameplay too because sometimes the game doesn't give you the chance to
name an item even if you wanted to.)

